WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.640
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.150
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed. Do they want to protect themselves? Other people?

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.830
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.780
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.410
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.490
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.860
Your grudge shall be released.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:16.070
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:19.950
and the listed sponsors.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.060
No! Stop!

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.300
No! Don’t pull that!

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.330
Don’t pull that string!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.450
Why?!

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.540
Get the proper person to come at once.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.940
Yes. Me?

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.850
I’m the nurse at Saigawara Middle School.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.370
My name is Shibata.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.040
Shibata Tsugumi.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.560
Then I’m counting on you.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.950
If you go, you won’t be able to come back.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.810
You can see? That?

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.540
You can stay in bed until next period.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.160
Shibata-sensei,

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.060
during the Six-Scripted Lantern Festival,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.030
you were able to see the entryway to Hell, right?

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:49.690
Who knows?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.380
You did say that if I went, I wouldn’t have been able to come back, right?

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.430
I don’t remember…

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.430
Shibata-sensei, do you know about it?

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.340
About Jigoku Shoujo?

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.450
Seems like my senses have been failing.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.160
Who knew she was in a place like this?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.530
Shibata Tsugumi.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.210
She apparently came to this school last year.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:29.200
Since, for a long time, she hasn’t interfered in Hell Sending,

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:33.220
I thought she was living normally somewhere, but…

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.270
Hajime-chan, I wonder what he’s doing?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.150
The father, eh?

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.800
I’ve determined the approximate location.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.840
Where the person who wrote, but erased, Shibata Tsugumi's name on the Hell Correspondence is.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.090
Why would anyone send that girl to Hell?

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.940
And what kind of place is it? Well?

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.970
Right now, Yama-waro is there.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.470
What?

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:00.280
Then?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.060
Is that with him too?

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.960
Someone seems to have bought what used to be in ruins at the beginning of this year.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.590
The dealer said there was construction here for a few months, but…

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.250
It’s so shabby!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.390
So peculiar? So peculiar?

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.010
Hime! No!

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.990
It hasn’t even been sent yet!

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.580
I’m just going to see what’s up!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.480
Your things are all mine.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.980
I want to try out Hell’s instructions!

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:34.190
Where does she learn those kinds of things?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.250
Are you alright?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.340
Hime!

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.750
I couldn’t pass through it!

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.260
How strange.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.100
Is this barrier too strong for us?

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.940
Yup. No change here.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.320
How about over there?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.590
Is father fine?

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:05.920
Really!

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.860
No, it's not like I had specific business.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:26.510
Ai. You’ve returned again.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.670
Yes, Grandma.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.990
Ai, is that what you were hoping for?

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.250
I've gotten used to being lonely, so…

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.510
But I do want you to come back soon.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:51.010
Oh no, nope, it’s nothing, so don’t mind.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.420
Hajime-chan, isn’t it strange?

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.580
Seems like I’ve been submitted to the Hell Correspondence.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.330
That might be appropriate.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.930
Rather than being on the wrong side,

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.790
that’s a lot more desirable.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.770
You are Shibata Tsugumi-sama, correct?

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:34.100
Who are you?

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:38.490
I’ve come as a servant for a person named Mizorogi, and I’m called Kikyou.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.640
Mizorogi said he would, by all means, like to see you, Shibata-sama.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.640
I am not interested.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.320
It’s about what’s written in this book.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:59.390
This book that’s said to be the only book approaching the truth about Jigoku Shoujo.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:02.340
It was written by your father, yes?

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:09.480
Hence I would like you to join us by all means.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:19.270
Why has Shibata-sensei been written into the Hell Correspondence?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.000
Why have you come?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.710
To stop us?

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.760
What are you saying Shibata-sensei has done?

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:51.940
My duty is to fulfill the desire of someone who wants to send someone to Hell.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.470
Don’t you consider anything?

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.660
Whether it’s good to send them, or?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:00.240
It’s not right!

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.740
I don’t really understand, but it’s wrong!

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.740
It's…

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.580
But what shall we do?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:16.290
According to Yama-waro, we can’t enter this mansion with our powers.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:19.780
That reminds me, where have Yama-waro and Kikuri gone?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.300
Really!

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.330
Shibata-sensei!

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.780
Long time no see.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.290
Long time no see,

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.490
Tsugumi.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.760
What?

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.040
Looks like we’re all here.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.490
Then I’ll guide you inside.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.500
Wait a second!

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.200
Shibata-sensei!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.680
Your name was written into the Hell Correspondence!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.970
I know.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.790
It’s kind of stuffy in here.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.220
This is what Yama-waro was talking about, eh?

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.220
Wait!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:26.430
It’s the things that look like Elekiters!

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:30.760
Oh! Ojou!

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.730
It’s best not to approach it!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.500
You want us to play with a toy like this?

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.390
That apparatus is the Reverser.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:55.210
It was an EMR apparatus that repulsed your supernatural powers.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:22.280
Did you call for me?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.990
Yes, I did call for you, Jigoku Shoujo.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.010
And Shibata Tsugumi-san.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:38.520
Have we met before?

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:39.920
No.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.410
Tsugumi-san, please sit in that chair.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:55.580
What are you trying to do?!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.510
Sensei!

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.870
Are you trying to send her to Hell?

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.700
What kind of grudge do you have against her?

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:05.810
In truth, I have no grudge against her.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:10.520
Well more truthfully, I love and respect Tsugumi-san’s father,

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:14.760
the one who wrote this book, Shibata Hajime-shi.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.480
This guy’s strange.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.910
Without a strong sense of hatred,

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:23.260
it should be impossible to access the Hell Correspondence!

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.680
Ah, if it’s about that, I’ll explain later.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.520
First, I’d like you to know what kind of person I am.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.260
Mizorogi Shougo.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:34.540
Applied Mathematician.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:38.550
Twenty years ago, he discovered what came to be known as the Mizorogi Constant,

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.930
which makes high probability space prediction possible.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:43.750
Afterward, he cut himself off from the media.

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:49.650
The space prediction constant I discovered is by itself just a formula,

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:53.750
but it was extremely effective in a specific field.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:58.930
It is thought that war from now on will be fought using unmanned weapons.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.000
Because the risk is thereby smaller.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.170
The space prediction constant…

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:07.510
It was, in the military field, very effective.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.780
People’s lives are calculations, too?

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:17.060
It became clear that my constant made the potential of unmanned attack planes comparatively higher.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:25.600
The character known as Mizorogi Shougo and his constant were bought up by a business.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.570
I was content with this.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.100
If I did not come out into the world, I could live the rest of my life as I liked it.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:38.580
However, I noticed my constant was making another, different thing clear.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:44.040
Separate from this real world, there exist other invisible worlds.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:48.720
In other words, this means that Hell in fact, exists.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:56.080
The formula proves the existence of Hell.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.530
My heart was stolen by this fact.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:02.160
Why is my heart so captivated by Hell?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:05.100
After a while, I finally remembered.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:16.150
The household I was brought up in, first of all, could not be said not to be Hell.

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:19.410
After all, this is entirely a metaphor.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:32.110
However, my mother said she sent my father to Hell,

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:36.610
and as a child, I could not understand her words very well.

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:41.580
My mother, too, disappeared after a few years.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.890
Hell.

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:48.640
There, there are those who send people to Hell, and are sent to Hell.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:53.520
In this world after Heisenberg, where the absolute is no longer absolute,

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:58.590
how appealing was the absolute existence of Hell!

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:04.070
I studied Hell Sending.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:09.440
Of course, I got a basic understanding from Shibata Hajime-shi’s book.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.400
In the past, the newspaper’s three-column advertisement.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.740
A primitive BBS written in BASIC.

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.650
And then, the Internet.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:22.240
As time passed, transitioning to cell phones,

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.810
the basic nature of Jigoku Shoujo listening and receiving a grudge

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.770
has continued without change.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.740
From that long ago?

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:36.750
I discovered that Hell Sending has a tendency to concentrate in one area.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:41.060
It sometimes escalates until a city falls apart.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.780
That was horrible.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:46.760
That is occurring in Saigawara city.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:52.790
Then I discovered that Jigoku Shoujo received a body here again.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.670
And that Shibata Hajime’s daughter,

00:15:55.670 --> 00:16:01.740
Shibata Tsugumi, who has a deep involvement with Jigoku Shoujo, was actually in this city.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.470
You wanted to meet Jigoku Shoujo,

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.990
so you entered Shibata-sensei's name!

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:12.570
Yes. Since I knew that Jigoku Shoujo's straw doll incarnations serve her as followers,

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:18.430
and have supernatural powers, I made this mansion.

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:20.960
So that we could speak on equal terms.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.420
Something’s wrong with you.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.420
However, I fail to understand.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.010
You’ve already said before, but without a feeling of hatred.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:29.760
It should be impossible to access the Hell Correspondence!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:35.020
I wanted to know objectively of Hell’s existence.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:41.010
However there is no human on earth who I hate enough to send to Hell.

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:44.080
If only I could have created the emotion of hatred,

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:47.070
I would have been able to connect to the Hell Correspondence?

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.530
What did you do?

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.850
He is a hypnotherapist.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:17:00.640
I had the emotion of hatred planted onto my deep psychology.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:05.710
Artificial hatred, even going that far?

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:08.380
That’s wrong! Everyone!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.200
And so,

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.490
what did you want to prove?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:17.060
There is a contradiction in the existence of the Hell Sending system.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:22.310
For example, Hell Sending occurs regardless of whether the hatred is valid,

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.880
or from misunderstanding or wrongful blame.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.350
Ever since I was a child,

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:31.800
as a sign of people being sent to Hell, I have continued living,

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.510
hearing the sound of bells.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:40.760
No matter how mistaken that hatred was,

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:43.850
Jigoku Shoujo sends them to Hell.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.680
And I couldn’t stop it.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.910
Yes! You’re right! That’s why it’s mistaken!

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:52.930
You can’t send people to Hell!

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:59.150
Certainly, we have sent many people to Hell even while thinking it was ridiculous.

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:02.820
But, that's our job, so…

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.350
Don’t you consider anything?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.730
Things like that…

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.810
Do you think I didn’t think about it?

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:17.170
Curses are the last salvation weak people’s "ressentiment" can hold.

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:21.560
People evolved and supplemented Hell,

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.880
creating a system called "curses."

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:28.090
In other words, Hell is only a fabrication created by humans?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.190
It must be.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:34.890
For me, Hell must absolutely exist.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.900
The ultimate irrationality,

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:44.150
separate from the concepts of ethics or morality, which was created for the convenience of human society.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.150
That is absolutely what Hell is!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.900
Enma Ai.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.420
You are the very symbol of that irrationality.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.430
Jigoku Shoujo,

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:58.790
I wanted to meet you.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.800
I am not who you wanted to meet.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.000
What?

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.600
Ichimoku-ren.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.600
O-Ojou!

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:18.060
Is this what Jigoku Shoujo does?

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:21.690
I don’t want to participate in such an evil thing!

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.570
Shibata-sensei!

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:24.770
Sensei, you’re going to be sent to Hell!

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.740
Even though you have no sin!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.780
I’m not really without sin.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.280
I, too, Hajime-chan…

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.290
That’s why I don’t care if that happens.

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:42.210
I’ve gotten tired of being alone, after all.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.310
Sensei!

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.510
You know what happens if you pull that red string, right?

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.510
Of course.

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:59.060
In a short time, I also will be sent to Hell.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.280
There’s no reason for you to involve Tsugumi!

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:07.390
The hypnosis cast on me is ended using a keyword as a trigger.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:11.330
When that happens, fully look down upon me.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.030
Stop!

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:21.390
Would you like to die this once?

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:23.070
Ojou!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.640
I heard the trigger,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.900
but I have yet to pull the string.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.910
There were children, just as I thought.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:44.600
They pulled the string.

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:47.420
Kikyou! You!

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.370
Please forgive me.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:53.040
I discovered you were trying to send these children to Hell,

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:56.610
and I requested Hell Sending in the same way as you.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.220
In the depths of your heart,

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:03.770
you suffered because the constant which you discovered would take away lives without sin.

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:09.320
So you took in children whose parents were lost on the battlefield, and you brought them up.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.380
It’s hypocrisy.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:14.210
Yes. These children could not forgive you,

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:19.380
who made a weapon that indiscriminately takes away lives.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.880
You all?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.650
I see.

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.390
I am sorry.

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:30.650
Kikyou!

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.820
I'm leaving these children to you.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:45.490
Now I get to meet you again,

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.120
Mother.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:53.700
This hatred will ferry you to Hell.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.400
Shibata-sensei!

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:09.520
Maybe? Weren’t you the same?

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.030
As what?

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:18.030
Weren’t you also fated to become Jigoku Shoujo?

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:19.870
I wonder.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:25.660
It is fundamentally impossible to resist fate.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:27.540
I believe that.

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.540
What?

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:32.430
I don’t want to!

00:22:32.430 --> 00:22:34.430
What’s fate?!

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:38.620
Who chooses something like that?

00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:41.040
What should I do?

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:49.800
Note: Candle says Kikyou Shinji.

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:49.800
Your grudges shall be released.

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:21.650
Your name?

00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:23.350
Kikuchi Kaito.

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:27.160
Your current mother isn’t your real mother, right?

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:28.160
Yeah.

00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:30.780
But she was really nice to me.

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:33.980
But she changed.

00:24:33.980 --> 00:24:35.600
And then father, too.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.290
I was enduring it, but…

00:24:38.740 --> 00:24:40.460
It’s painful after all.

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:42.180
It’s sad.

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:44.630
So you?

00:24:45.470 --> 00:24:48.570
Next time: The Back’s Front

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:55.880
